  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Artist's book, consisting of text and printed lines, dots, triangles and other geometric figures bound in beige silk, with a triangle cut-out on the front cover, mounted title paper labels. Issued in a teal blue silk box with a five-sided cut-out with an etched acrylic "window" and an inlaid printed title paper label, magnetic closure, light blue printed paper lining.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Edition of 18 copies.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Inspired by Euclid's geometric postulate, 'Any two points can be joined by a straight line,' Connect the Dots explores, through words and images, the difficulties of applying scientific theory to an elusive relationship. Hoping that Euclid's postulate is right, the narrator imagines a landscape of constellations and trajectories, of dots and arcs, in an attempt to connect one person to another"--Artist's website, viewed on February 4, 2015.</subfield>
  </datafield>
